  "result": "The concept `drv.motion.entering_region` passed the gate on the first run (verdict **OK**, 3 witnesses, one atom read). I used 1 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n- **Body:** `.rises (.atom \"rel_occupies\" [x, r] [])`. `rises` means the overlap holds at this observation and did not at the one before, which is exactly what the contract asks for. A continuing overlap is not an entry. The result is unknown when either observation's overlap is unobserved or there is no earlier observation. The contract left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings.\n- **Witnesses:** region 100 is a lane from x=10 to 20 m and y=-2 to 2 m. Road user 1 is a motor vehicle heading east. Each trace has three observations 1 s apart, and every scenario is judged at t1 only.\n  - **holds:** x starts clear of the lane at x=5 and is at x=15 from t1 on, so the result is compliant.\n  - **fails:** x is inside the lane at every observation, so the result is violated.\n  - **blind:** the same positions as holds, with `rel.occupies` masked, so the result is unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
